{"title":"1995 IMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3b\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3b</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_7_from_Brilliant_Wiki_(Muirheads)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7 from Brilliant Wiki (Muirheads)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Solution_8_(fast_Titu&#39;s_Lemma_no_substitutions)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 8 (fast Titu's Lemma no substitutions)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Solution_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Solution_10_(Similar_to_others)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 10 (Similar to others)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Solution_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Solution_12\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 12</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Resources\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Resources</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(<i>Nazar Agakhanov, Russia</i>)\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/acc6d9a6172d35127b6cb37ea92192caf7029a54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> be positive real numbers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/3/2e32cfd3a6f5f31f73d0b272a5f7b1638fd16551.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" />. Prove that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2ad1ca4077a0191129259e27550780a3f1fdeb7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{a^3(b+c)} + \\frac{1}{b^3(c+a)} + \\frac{1}{c^3(a+b)} \\geq \\frac{3}{2}.\\]\" width=\"302\" height=\"42\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We make the substitution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/d/38d4b56c93b88c38a9429833dba4a868835cb3bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x= 1/a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/d/6edd21c95888bb46951c7d4c11c964d79dd55dfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=1/b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/1/f01a03a3869544d6b6fe869e6c10cd78a4d30698.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=1/c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" />.  Then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/f/90f3553f12087c1111e26f9a0eb166e70a59569e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\frac{1}{a^3(b+c)} + \\frac{1}{b^3(c+a)} + \\frac{1}{c^3(a+b)} &amp;= \\frac{x^3}{xyz(1/y+1/z)} + \\frac{y^3}{xyz(1/z+1/x)} + \\frac{z^3}{xyz(1/x+1/y)} \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{x^2}{y+z} + \\frac{y^2}{z+x} + \\frac{z^2}{x+y} . \\end{align*}\" width=\"704\" height=\"93\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/7/6675cecbbaf9310e54a431d566a2f298e134f7b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x^2,y^2,z^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/b/41b5b224c7f892062942ce4810bca7cd74b3ff6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigl( 1/(y+z), 1/(z+x), 1/(x+y) \\bigr)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"252\" height=\"22\" /> are similarly sorted sequences, it follows from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rearrangement_Inequality\" title=\"Rearrangement Inequality\">Rearrangement Inequality</a> that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/4/71403fe6c3b75ffcba1b9a6b5f971de6b55c5646.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{x^2}{y+z} + \\frac{y^2}{z+x} + \\frac{z^2}{x+y} \\ge \\frac{1}{2} \\left( \\frac{y^2+z^2}{y+z} + \\frac{z^2+x^2}{z+x} + \\frac{x^2+y^2}{x+y} \\right) .\\]\" width=\"476\" height=\"43\" />\nBy the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Power_Mean_Inequality\" title=\"Power Mean Inequality\">Power Mean Inequality</a>,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/9/989e5d36ba7cf851d81f7088af37520e37e6660a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{y^2+z^2}{y+z} \\ge \\frac{(y+z)^2}{2(x+y)} = \\frac{x+y}{2} .\\]\" width=\"225\" height=\"43\" />\nSymmetric application of this argument yields\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/0/620e97434e940e9b19e517b4b2c6cf54650b2fac.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2}\\left( \\frac{y^2+z^2}{y+z} + \\frac{z^2+x^2}{z+x} + \\frac{x^2+y^2}{x+y} \\right) \\ge \\frac{1}{2}(x+y+z) .\\]\" width=\"395\" height=\"43\" />\nFinally, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AM-GM\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"AM-GM\">AM-GM</a> gives us\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/2/e42cbff4cc7e3201d23320fafdd22e3394fe6b79.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2}(x+y+z) \\ge \\frac{3}{2}xyz = \\frac{3}{2},\\]\" width=\"207\" height=\"37\" />\nas desired.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We make the same substitution as in the first solution.  We note that in general,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/4/3146d0276a6a7a9d0bd6add8d06b2fe06eef77d0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{p}{q+r} = \\frac{(p+q+r)}{(p+q+r)-p} - 1 .\\]\" width=\"221\" height=\"43\" />\nIt follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/3/c73ed093cc73a8d9a14185fa525e7067e5c3725d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y,z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/b/e5b219fb55427223c8089702f282eb284b7a3a95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigl(x/(y+z), y/(z+x), z/(x+y)\\bigr)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"253\" height=\"22\" /> are similarly sorted sequences.  Then by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Chebyshev%27s_Inequality\" title=\"Chebyshev&#39;s Inequality\">Chebyshev's Inequality</a>,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/0/960246406323c7a24b7d4b30de719ac19185d4a6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{x^2}{y+z} + \\frac{y^2}{z+x} + \\frac{z^2}{x+y} \\ge \\frac{1}{3}(x+y+z) \\left(\\frac{x}{y+z} + \\frac{y}{z+x} + \\frac{z}{x+y} \\right) .\\]\" width=\"489\" height=\"43\" />\nBy AM-GM, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/5/0a506c810ebf1de3dac76d42a30ba27ea2ba604a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x+y+z}{3} \\ge \\sqrt[3]{xyz}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"179\" height=\"35\" />, and by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nesbitt%27s_Inequality\" title=\"Nesbitt&#39;s Inequality\">Nesbitt's Inequality</a>,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/3/77361d35df2f5dcf218278163941fae8e1a37bb0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{x}{y+z} + \\frac{y}{z+x} + \\frac{z}{x+y} \\ge \\frac{3}{2}.\\]\" width=\"220\" height=\"41\" />\nThe desired conclusion follows.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Without clever substitutions:\nBy Cauchy-Schwarz, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/9/8e9f60ffd3a0c08d5fc57bbe33ab40f6716fb90c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\sum_{cyc}\\dfrac{1}{a^3 (b+c)}\\right)\\left(\\sum_{cyc}a(b+c)\\right)\\geq \\left( \\dfrac{1}{a}+\\dfrac{1}{b}+\\dfrac{1}{c}\\right) ^2=(ab+ac+bc)^2\\]\" width=\"512\" height=\"54\" /> Dividing by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/e/92e1e8a2f66d597d75dae759eb58f3e5cb8a9bdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(ab+bc+ac)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"120\" height=\"20\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/1/d318f9f999662cc4e122acfe0e489e7b82d14f12.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{1}{a^3 (b+c)}+\\dfrac{1}{b^3 (a+c)}+\\dfrac{1}{c^3 (a+b)}\\geq \\dfrac{1}{2}(ab+bc+ac)\\geq \\dfrac{3}{2}\\]\" width=\"444\" height=\"42\" /> by AM-GM.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3b\">Solution 3b</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3b\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Without clever notation:\nBy Cauchy-Schwarz, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/1/de1b72ffacd69948c0c8cd4e345810ad5bf77fb8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(a(b+c) + b(c+a) + c(a+b)\\right) \\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{a^3 (b+c)} + \\frac{1}{b^3 (c+a)} + \\frac{1}{c^3 (a+b)}\\right)\\]\" width=\"533\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/d/90da8812edc4026ceee1ad86c3cbc323d206abfa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\ge \\left(\\frac{1}{a} + \\frac{1}{b} + \\frac{1}{c}\\right)^2\\]\" width=\"134\" height=\"46\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/5/c851614b559da7d06e8170306682386770028213.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= (ab + bc + ac)^2\\]\" width=\"133\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Dividing by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/2/e22daa57b6fc1847f34f8663e70fe249513e4b04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(ab + bc + ac)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"116\" height=\"18\" /> and noting that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/b/6cb33253f6e0925fda1fc0a8467d29b52095ac6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab + bc + ac \\ge 3(a^2b^2c^2)^{\\frac{1}{3}} = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"233\" height=\"22\" /> by AM-GM gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/4/d54776a9a8bf696304617198439effde7bd07472.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{a^3 (b+c)} + \\frac{1}{b^3 (c+a)} + \\frac{1}{c^3 (a+b)} \\ge \\frac{ab + bc + ac}{2} \\ge \\frac{3}{2},\\]\" width=\"426\" height=\"42\" />\nas desired.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>After the setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/6/46667f8477dab0803c575bb144cce8b1f1e5b843.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\frac{1}{x}, b=\\frac{1}{y}, c=\\frac{1}{z},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"159\" height=\"40\" /> and as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/5/175cbe9f31961b36429a43d532d7bf12d2342d13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/8/638bbd0153c23e386e0f05aa642cc5d94f127f2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{1}{a}\\cdot\\frac{1}{b}\\cdot\\frac{1} {c}=1\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"122\" height=\"43\" /> concluding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5bcb4dcda1cfb0470f1125444463ff427bdb112.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x y z=1 .$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/4/234ef54a60e3f564fb7066f456083300ae1723ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textsf{Claim}:$\" width=\"48\" height=\"11\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/06534facad7e3ba4c63efe736bfdbf52f6087220.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{x^{2}}{y+z}+\\frac{y^{2}}{z+x}+\\frac{z^{2}}{x+y} \\geq \\frac{3}{2}\\]\" width=\"215\" height=\"42\" />\nBy Titu Lemma,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/2/7427bd3408c33626b4a5f1f4fccf7dd5f24a9a0b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies\\frac{x^{2}}{y+z}+\\frac{y^{2}}{z+x}+\\frac{z^{2}}{x+y} \\geq \\frac{(x+y+z)^{2}}{2(x+y+z)}\\]\" width=\"343\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/a/dfa01fde2adc0106b6f15dbfcbec99c58b04a522.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies\\frac{x^{2}}{y+z}+\\frac{y^{2}}{z+x}+\\frac{z^{2}}{x+y} \\geq \\frac{(x+y+z)}{2}\\]\" width=\"334\" height=\"42\" />\nNow by AM-GM we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/9/9b9e65b2e49545753b9433f13de2ea441ebecff8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x+y+z)\\geq3\\sqrt[3]{xyz}\\]\" width=\"165\" height=\"19\" />and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/4/1d4e962c8ab321be15667f8986436dc8f4e42c11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xyz=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"15\" /> which concludes to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/f/54fecdc73023b17261c3348aef834afad78025fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies  (x+y+z)\\geq3\\sqrt[3]{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"191\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Therefore we get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/8/b38826e887974ed7738ac4f343433382cd2985a5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies\\frac{x^{2}}{y+z}+\\frac{y^{2}}{z+x}+\\frac{z^{2}}{x+y} \\geq \\frac{3}{2}\\]\" width=\"255\" height=\"42\" />Hence our claim is proved ~~ Aritra12\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Proceed as in Solution 1, to arrive at the equivalent inequality\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/c/dbcd9ee9a9b8cbe8e8cfefd302fd209867addac6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{x^2}{y+z} + \\frac{y^2}{z+x} + \\frac{z^2}{x+y} \\ge \\frac{3}{2} .\\]\" width=\"220\" height=\"43\" />\nBut we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/4/df40b592e8b599c7f586c15854c5a1cc9cddf5cb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x + y + z \\ge 3xyz = 3\\]\" width=\"168\" height=\"15\" /> by AM-GM. Furthermore,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/0/570509feef6ef70bfd314c5494d350178ed99627.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x + y + y + z + x + z) (\\frac{x^2}{y+z} + \\frac{y^2}{z+x} + \\frac{z^2}{x+y}) \\ge (x + y + z)^2\\]\" width=\"477\" height=\"42\" />\nby Cauchy-Schwarz, and so dividing by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/8/ab898303770fe82dec24932766c2be77cab2569c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(x + y + z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"99\" height=\"20\" /> gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/0/4901d3782183356dfb861e16fef1a21c9f918429.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}\\frac{x^2}{y+z} + \\frac{y^2}{z+x} + \\frac{z^2}{x+y} &amp;\\ge \\frac{(x + y + z)}{2} \\\\ &amp;\\ge \\frac{3}{2} \\end{align*}\" width=\"294\" height=\"86\" />\nas desired.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Without clever substitutions, and only AM-GM!\n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/5/cb5aae09dfc65620147cd4d025f7d4873c9b22d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc = 1 \\implies a = \\frac{1}{bc}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"160\" height=\"37\" />. The cyclic sum becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/9/1b9ac16f839b3666fa842189801fae8b1b7481b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{cyc}\\frac{(bc)^3}{b + c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"68\" height=\"49\" />. Note that by AM-GM, the cyclic sum is greater than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/8/b081fed47cb2992a5c5111f5d396d04d56aba7b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\left(\\frac{1}{(a+b)(b+c)(a+c)}\\right)^{\\frac13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"210\" height=\"49\" />. We now see that we have the three so we must be on the right path. We now only need to show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6eb26f10f6b37e12f542f22e4c8dbefd717940a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac32 \\geq 3\\left(\\frac{1}{(a+b)(b+c)(a+c)}\\right)^\\frac13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"247\" height=\"49\" />. Notice that by AM-GM, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/6/12691fa4faa5a226aade5eca5c7e21f8ed09e1cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b \\geq 2\\sqrt{ab}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/5/175b15b42234de4d68d5514fe8f804efed653210.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b + c \\geq 2\\sqrt{bc}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"102\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/2/c72ed5363e5601848b28e5219649c7d523591159.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + c \\geq 2\\sqrt{ac}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"105\" height=\"18\" />. Thus, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/c/d0c7cf28e700e9ebef9597ae365649abf74f94b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+b)(b+c)(a+c) \\geq 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"192\" height=\"18\" />, concluding that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/9/1e9ca0e2803a7156fa582243d0afd2d397d35916.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{cyc} \\frac{(bc)^3}{b+c} \\geq \\frac32 \\geq 3\\left(\\frac{1}{(a+b)(b+c)(a+c)}\\right)^{\\frac13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"342\" height=\"54\" />.\n</p><p>^ This solution is incorrect, as it does not prove inequalities in the right direction. Proving that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/7/dd783a8be259d36e8a5e03cde7f7429d05dcec38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A \\geq B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/0/ec0c4121874898571a64afd6cc437b2723c431fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C \\geq B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"17\" /> does not show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/1/8c1b7c3a9fc1ab556141cdc3dbdd0cfed2241bbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A \\geq C \\geq B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"93\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_7_from_Brilliant_Wiki_.28Muirheads.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7_from_Brilliant_Wiki_(Muirheads)\">Solution 7 from Brilliant Wiki (Muirheads)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7 from Brilliant Wiki (Muirheads)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://brilliant.org/wiki/muirhead-inequality/\">https://brilliant.org/wiki/muirhead-inequality/</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_8_.28fast_Titu.27s_Lemma_no_substitutions.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_8_(fast_Titu's_Lemma_no_substitutions)\">Solution 8 (fast Titu's Lemma no substitutions)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 8 (fast Titu&#39;s Lemma no substitutions)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Rewrite <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/4/3a48b533b5dda8e6e149ed4fb6cc65446a55e3dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{a^3(b+c)} + \\frac{1}{b^3(a+c)} + \\frac{1}{c^3(a+b)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"266\" height=\"43\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/8/968026020eee60f7e4fb20986d23521b7b1f7a24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(1/a)^2}{a(b+c)} + \\frac{(1/b)^2}{b(a+c)} + \\frac{(1/c)^2}{c(a+b)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"243\" height=\"45\" />. \n</p><p>Now applying Titu's lemma yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/4/d3442e5407f2b634448d210c99c0f99cb149c1dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(1/a)^2}{a(b+c)} + \\frac{(1/b)^2}{b(a+c)} + \\frac{(1/c)^2}{c(a+b)} \\geq \\frac{(\\frac{1}{a} + \\frac{1}{b} + \\frac{1}{c})^2}{a(b+c) + b(a+c) + c(a+b)} = \\frac{(ab + bc + ca)^2}{2(ab + bc + ca)} = \\frac{ab + bc + ca}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"770\" height=\"47\" />. \n</p><p>Now applying the AM-GM inequality on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/2/422cf05ec47279f834ab2bccc9f05fa623a89531.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab + bc +ca \\geq 3((abc)^2)^{\\frac{1}{3}} = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"235\" height=\"24\" />. The result now follows.\n</p><p>Note: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/7/e871f5fb470af432b407b195a651dcd119d0b724.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab + bc + ca = \\frac{1}{a} + \\frac{1}{b} + \\frac{1}{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"205\" height=\"38\" />, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/3/2e32cfd3a6f5f31f73d0b272a5f7b1638fd16551.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" />. (Why? Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/2/0e283ba74ba084d490920199ee68fa7729978910.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\frac{1}{bc}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"55\" height=\"38\" />, and hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/b/2fbe8819f9cff6262183a737c748612e2c45f507.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{a} = bc$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"55\" height=\"38\" />).\n</p><p>~th1nq3r\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_9\">Solution 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ol><li><ol><li>Inequality Proof</li></ol></li></ol>\n<p>We want to prove that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/0/480c1f257d75f614a77d72fb13b516bfb5cb79d9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{a^3(b+c)}+\\frac{1}{b^3(c+a)}+\\frac{1}{c^3(a+b)} \\geq \\frac{3}{2}\\]\" width=\"297\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/3/2e32cfd3a6f5f31f73d0b272a5f7b1638fd16551.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>---\n</p>\n<ul><li><ul><li>Step 1. Substitution.**</li></ul></li></ul>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/3/07383216724928111b3f14932aa2f7bc629da90b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{1}{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"50\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/2/06262edfd28be2c9dd35ad3d3e97c171ad9db341.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac{1}{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"49\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/3/583f7e51546225cd3618bff7bb145abe52c85143.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = \\frac{1}{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"48\" height=\"38\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/8/108d7c42600b1f1ea04d17fb59a2e501130ad353.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xyz = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"17\" />, and \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/3/693bfe8a711b2969344d3b09f058012f43b4458c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{a^3(b+c)} = \\frac{x^2}{y+z}, \\quad \\frac{1}{b^3(c+a)} = \\frac{y^2}{z+x}, \\quad \\frac{1}{c^3(a+b)} = \\frac{z^2}{x+y}\\]\" width=\"475\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p>So the inequality becomes \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/652e1a41ba21a798b6cbbbec1263f43615f05cd2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{x^2}{y+z}+\\frac{y^2}{z+x}+\\frac{z^2}{x+y} \\geq \\frac{3}{2}\\]\" width=\"215\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>---\n</p>\n<ul><li><ul><li>Step 2. AM-GM proof.**</li></ul></li></ul>\n<p>Multiplying through by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/c/20c873f11eae6cf8f88b10ac5cb96db9eb7fd642.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x + y)(y + z)(z + x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"169\" height=\"20\" />, it is equivalent to \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/1/12113b9f79dc55a5e02a6e0eb7c2e7c730cd3044.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2(x+y)(x+z) + y^2(y+z)(y+x) + z^2(z+x)(z+y) \\geq \\frac{3}{2}(x+y)(y+z)(z+x)\\]\" width=\"545\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Expanding shows that we need \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/9/f39389fdce29867c2f02e52abfa3461546228edf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{2}{3}\\left(x^4+y^4+z^4+x^3y+\\cdots+z^2xy\\right) \\geq x^2y+x^2z+y^2x+y^2z+z^2x+z^2y+2xyz\\]\" width=\"586\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Now apply AM-GM in groups, for example \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/c/40c63e4f6cbd669159f66d583b70509a9732094d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{x^4+x^3y+y^3z}{3}\\geq x^2y, \\quad \\frac{y^4+y^3z+z^3x}{3}\\geq y^2z\\]\" width=\"363\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>and similarly for the other four symmetric terms, plus \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/d/fcda2d4f006b1df18c828d564a8a0b12eb17e1fe.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{2(x^2yz+y^2zx+z^2xy)}{3}\\geq 2xyz\\]\" width=\"241\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Adding all these inequalities gives exactly the required result.\n</p><p>---\n</p>\n<ul><li><ul><li>Conclusion:** Therefore,</li></ul></li></ul>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/0/480c1f257d75f614a77d72fb13b516bfb5cb79d9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{a^3(b+c)}+\\frac{1}{b^3(c+a)}+\\frac{1}{c^3(a+b)} \\geq \\frac{3}{2}\\]\" width=\"297\" height=\"41\" /> ∎\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_10_.28Similar_to_others.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_10_(Similar_to_others)\">Solution 10 (Similar to others)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 10 (Similar to others)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that the sums are cyclic so without loss of generality assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/3/bf30839a9c4662e1f0f6e4de7b042ea58c342d68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c \\le b \\le a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"73\" height=\"15\" />. Determine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accc80fdf164cef264f56a82b6f9f6add320fe05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/f/a2f653792d3ec212baddeca744d3636f572668a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{a}, \\frac{1}{b}, \\frac{1}{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"58\" height=\"38\" /> respectively. It follows <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/5/1d534e199fa536c255a869fc05ba3afd636623de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\le y \\le z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" /> and \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/9/dd9e7739d00e1d2fcf2125e20cd8fbb8cc765ec5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{\\text{cyc}} \\frac{x^2}{y+z}\\]\" width=\"72\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>By the Rearrangement Inequality:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/0/150e495eb3cabdcd866ca820c98a0dcc07d56ee0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{\\text{cyc}} \\frac{x^2}{y+z} \\ge \\sum_{\\text{cyc}} \\frac{xy}{y+z}\\]\" width=\"169\" height=\"49\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/4/eb4bc587f347c8fd16f9facfb009501a797aedb6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{\\text{cyc}} \\frac{x^2}{y+z} \\ge \\sum_{\\text{cyc}} \\frac{xz}{y+z}\\]\" width=\"169\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>Determine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/8/1c8f402c49e9319005763f2b611d197d27b05e52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = \\sum_{\\text{cyc}} \\frac{x^2}{y+z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"112\" height=\"53\" />. Adding both yields\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/1/74182dab2d9353906e72580222a0a5ec112c8c5c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2S \\ge x+y+z \\ge 3 \\sqrt[3]{xyz} \\ge 3\\]\" width=\"230\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/5/4656798fc48e0677ebfa9bdc9f7d0314a39e348b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S \\ge \\frac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"51\" height=\"38\" /> as desired. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p><p>Scroll all the way down\n<i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_11\">Solution 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/3/2e32cfd3a6f5f31f73d0b272a5f7b1638fd16551.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" />, we can multiply each numerator by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/d/a2d179ae5c54f9d56332b1be01890f1eb3550fb5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(abc)^2 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"82\" height=\"21\" />. This gives:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/4/534709b25e0127433595212ab1a02cba09338e71.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a^2b^2c^2}{a^3(b+c)} + \\frac{a^2b^2c^2}{b^3(c+a)} + \\frac{a^2b^2c^2}{c^3(a+b)} = \\frac{(bc)^2}{ab+ac} + \\frac{(ac)^2}{bc+ab} + \\frac{(ab)^2}{ac+bc}\\]\" width=\"508\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p>Applying Titu's Lemma, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/e/bfed1cf5695591831815833f4f9091d58c0220d6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{(bc)^2}{ab+ac} + \\frac{(ac)^2}{bc+ab} + \\frac{(ab)^2}{ac+bc} \\geq \\frac{(bc+ac+ab)^2}{(ab+ac) + (bc+ab) + (ac+bc)} = \\frac{ab+bc+ac}{2}\\]\" width=\"610\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p>Finally, by AM-GM and the condition <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/5/175cbe9f31961b36429a43d532d7bf12d2342d13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/9/159656cfca66c36f4531af051e4fd5a6780b6c0e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{ab+bc+ac}{2} \\geq \\frac{3\\sqrt[3]{a^2b^2c^2}}{2} = \\frac{3}{2}\\]\" width=\"233\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>as desired. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n~ Ethanluyixuan2012\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_12\">Solution 12</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 12\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/5/175cbe9f31961b36429a43d532d7bf12d2342d13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" />, the given inequality is equivalent to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/9/8d97a76241a06f34c3eb5d6731ef57334901efdc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{bc}{a^2(b+c)} + \\frac{ca}{b^2(a+c)} + \\frac{ab}{c^2(a+b)} \\ge \\frac{3}{2}\\]\" width=\"297\" height=\"42\" />\nWe see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/4/1449bce7ed3429f8b77c4f53c651d7e47cd3494a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$bc\\le ca\\le ab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"101\" height=\"17\" />. Also, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c35a4bb9bc40390de60bd90843dd30dc05acfbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2b+a^2c\\ge ab^2+b^2c\\ge c^2b+ac^2\\implies\\frac{1}{a^2(b+c)}\\le \\frac{1}{b^2(c+a)}\\le\\frac{1}{c^2(a+b)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"580\" height=\"43\" />. By Rearrangement Inequality, \n\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{bc}{a^2(b+c)} + \\frac{ca}{b^2(a+c)} + \\frac{ab}{c^2(a+b)} &amp;\\ge \\frac{ca}{a^2(b+c)}+\\frac{ab}{b^2(a+c)}+\\frac{bc}{c^2(a+b)}\\\\\n\\frac{bc}{a^2(b+c)} + \\frac{ca}{b^2(a+c)} + \\frac{ab}{c^2(a+b)}&amp;\\ge \\frac{ab}{a^2(b+c)}+\\frac{bc}{b^2(a+c)}+\\frac{ca}{c^2(a+b)}\n\\end{align*}\nIt follows that\n\\begin{align*}\n&amp; \\,\\quad 2\\left(\\frac{bc}{a^2(b+c)}+\\frac{ca}{b^2(a+c)}+\\frac{ab}{c^2(a+b)}\\right)\\\\\n&amp;\\ge \\frac{c}{a(b+c)}+\\frac{a}{b(a+c)}+\\frac{b}{c(a+b)} + \\frac{b}{a(b+c)}+\\frac{c}{b(a+c)}+\\frac{a}{c(a+b)}\\\\\n&amp;=\\frac{1}{a}+\\frac{1}{b}+\\frac{1}{c}\\\\\n&amp;\\ge \\frac{3}{\\sqrt[3]{abc}}\\\\\n&amp;=3\n\\end{align*}\nOr <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/4/1f4f753957fb1aa404b24dd77529a8ac9a38c4c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{bc}{a^2(b+c)}+\\frac{ca}{b^2(a+c)}+\\frac{ab}{c^2(a+b)}\\ge \\frac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"303\" height=\"44\" />, as desired.\n</p><p>~Pieandpi31415926535897932\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1995 IMO Problems\">1995 IMO Problems</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.mathlinks.ro/Forum/viewtopic.php?p=365178#p365178\">Discussion on AoPS/MathLinks</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO\" title=\"1995 IMO\">1995 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1995 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1995 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1995 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1995 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1995 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1995 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1995 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1995 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017185345\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.058 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.079 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 603/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1238/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 22114/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   16.632      1 -total\n 47.69%    7.931      1 Template